@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title POST external_accounts: verified connect und bootstrap

autonumber
actor "Der Client" as Client
participant "REST / RestAlchemy controller" as API
participant "Zulip" as Zulip
database "Account / encrypted credential / identity / outbox" as DB
participant "Bridge account coordinator" as Bridge
participant "Private Workspace API\ncurrent realm mTLS" as PrivateAPI
database "Ready public events" as Events
participant "WebSocket dispatcher" as WS

Client -> API : POST current request (api_key write-only)
API -> Zulip : validate credential
Zulip --> API : verified realm_uuid/user_id/delivery_email
API -> DB : account + encrypted credential + verified link + outbox
API --> Client : 201 sanitized status=connecting

DB -> Bridge : account desired-state task
Bridge -> PrivateAPI : mTLS client certificate\nclaim account
PrivateAPI -> DB : authorize current identity generation\nsticky assignment + account lease generation
PrivateAPI --> Bridge : server-owned account scope + lease generation
Bridge -> Zulip : register queue(supported events)
alt registration success
  Zulip --> Bridge : boundary
  Bridge -> Bridge : start sequential realtime
  Bridge -> PrivateAPI : mTLS ensure history root after boundary
  PrivateAPI -> DB : idempotent history root
else registration failure
  Zulip --> Bridge : transient failure
  Bridge -> Bridge : backoff; no history root
end

DB -> Events : external_account.created with projection transaction
WS -> Events : replay/live
WS -> Client : current-contract event

note over API,DB
  Email is candidate, not ownership proof.
  api_key is encrypted and never returned/logged.
  Maximum one Zulip account per Workspace user.
  Heartbeat 10s; degraded 30s; offline 60s.
end note

note over Bridge,PrivateAPI
  mTLS authenticates realm/provider/instance/identity generation.
  Account lease is a separate authorization fence.
end note
@enduml
